meta {
  name: CreateWorkspace
  type: grpc
  seq: 1
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.HierarchyService/CreateWorkspace
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "name": "csptech",
      "key": "CSP",
      "description": "An example workspace",
      "tags": ["customer", "active"],
      "idempotency_key": "{{$guid}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0017, convention 5). The `ctx` field the messages still declare is ignored
  by the server — do not use it: it gives the false impression of scoping the
  call.

  A lean registration on purpose: a name, a key, a description and tags. A
  workspace groups projects — the one that configures a repository is the project.
}
